{
  "_comment": [
    "Geographic fund-flow universe. Each region is a BASKET of US-listed",
    "country/regional ETFs. Flows are aggregated in dollars across the whole",
    "basket, so the region row answers 'how much money moved into this",
    "geography', not 'how did one ticker trade'.",
    "",
    "  etf       — primary vehicle. Its price series drives the price-momentum",
    "              overlay (flow-vs-price confirmation / divergence).",
    "  basket    — every vehicle whose dollars count toward the region. Always",
    "              includes the primary. Deliberately includes both broad and",
    "              thematic sleeves (e.g. China = MCHI broad + FXI large-cap +",
    "              KWEB internet) because rotation BETWEEN sleeves is itself a",
    "              flow signal.",
    "  hedged    — currency-hedged twin, where a liquid one exists. Used to",
    "              decompose FX drag out of the unhedged USD return.",
    "  bloc      — grouping for the summary narrative roll-up."
  ],
